---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

/**
 * Handles are rendered as small middot-separated links (.chips), because a
 * run of twenty accounts reads as a list and not as twenty sentences.
 */
const instagram = [
	'technologyreview',
	'symmetry_magazine',
	'quantamag',
	'unseenmp',
	'gowithsameer',
	'indiahiddengems',
	'historycoolkids',
	'history.asitis',
	'indialostandfound',
	'brownhistory',
	'betweenthelines20',
	'warmup',
	'areypatahai',
	'greatindianhustlers',
];

const reddit = [
	'todayilearned',
	'triviaoftheday',
	'Quizbowl',
	'history',
	'HistoryMemes',
	'HistoryPorn',
	'AajMaineJana',
	'MapPorn',
	'IndiaCricket',
	'neutrinos',
	'Damnthatsinteresting',
	'interestingasfuck',
	'helm',
];

const films = [
	'The Dark Knight',
	'Inception',
	'Interstellar',
	'The Martian',
	'Oppenheimer',
	'The Theory of Everything',
	'The Social Network',
	'The Wolf of Wall Street',
	'Iron Man',
	'Spider-Man 2',
	'Spider-Man: Brand New Day',
	'Across the Spider-Verse',
	'Star Wars V',
	'Back to the Future',
	'The Matrix',
	'Dune',
	'Cars 2',
	'Toy Story 3',
];
---

<Base
	title="Beyond"
	description="Quizzing, films, travel and food — the other half, and the resources behind a decade of quizzing."
>

	<header class="wrap page-head">
		<h1>Things I do to keep my creativity fresh</h1>
		<p class="lede">Most of it comes back to the same thing: I like knowing where things come from. That is what quizzing rewards, it is most of why I read history, and it is not far off what makes a physics problem fun (I think!)</p>
	</header>

	<section class="wrap block prose" id="quizzing">
		<h2>Quizzing</h2>

		<p>I have been at this since class six. If you have never done it: a quiz question is a set of hints that only resolve if you connect them, and the pleasure is almost entirely in the moment they click. Getting there needs a wide and fairly undisciplined reading habit, history, geography, science, sport, film, music, whatever is in front of me, which is a hobby I would have anyway lol</p>
		<p>I have quizzed at school, college and national level, and currently part of IITB Quizzing Team. My genres are India, history and mythology, sci-tech, and sport!</p>

		<h3>Some good stuff</h3>

		<ul class="kit">
			<li>
				<span class="k">Wikipedia</span>
				<span>Still the best thing on the internet. The rabbit holes are not a distraction from the reading; they <em>are</em> the reading</span>
			</li>
			<li>
				<span class="k">Newspapers</span>
				<span>Used to do this in school but lost touch in undergrad</span>
			</li>
			<li>
				<span class="k">Sport</span>
				<span><a href="https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/tag/the-pulse/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">The Pulse</a> at The Athletic is the single best sports read going</span>
			</li>
			<li>
				<span class="k">Drilling</span>
				<span><a href="https://www.sporcle.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Sporcle</a>, a fun way to test knowledge</span>
			</li>
			<li>
				<span class="k">Instagram</span>
				<span>
					Accounts that are worth the algorithm:
					<span class="chips kit-chips">
						{instagram.map((h) => (
							<a class="chip" href={`https://www.instagram.com/${h}/`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">@{h}</a>
						))}
					</span>
				</span>
			</li>
			<li>
				<span class="k">Reddit</span>
				<span>
					And on the other tab:
					<span class="chips kit-chips">
						{reddit.map((r) => (
							<a class="chip" href={`https://www.reddit.com/r/${r}/`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">r/{r}</a>
						))}
					</span>
				</span>
			</li>
			<li>
				<span class="k">Long reads</span>
				<span>The <a href="https://iicdelhi.in/publications" target="_blank" rel="noopener">India International Centre</a> occasional publications are underrated. My picks: <span class="nums">OP 12, OP 13, OP 28, OP 32-33, OP 48</span></span>
			</li>
			<li>
				<span class="k">Odd corners</span>
				<span><a href="https://amul.com/topicals" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Amul topicals</a> are an accidental archive of Indian current affairs, and the <a href="https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">UNESCO World Heritage list</a> is worth knowing cold</span>
			</li>
		</ul>
	</section>

	<section class="wrap block prose" id="films">
		<h2>Films</h2>

		<p>I watch across genres, but what decides it for me is plot and cinematography, I want a film that makes me think and makes me feel, and I will forgive a lot if it does. That said, I am not going to pretend I do not love a good action film xD</p>

		<p class="muted list-intro">A shortlist, and it was hard to keep it this short :')</p>
		<p class="picks">{films.map((f, i) => (<><cite>{f}</cite>{i < films.length - 1 && <span class="sep"> · </span>}</>))}</p>
	</section>

	<section class="wrap block prose" id="travel">
		<h2>Travel and food</h2>

		<p>I travel whenever there is a gap in the calendar, and I have now covered most corners of India, the North-East is the conspicuous gap and has been at the top of the list for a while. The point is rarely the sight itself: it is meeting people, and eating their food, and working out why a place is the way it is. I am a foodie and a vegetarian, which sounds like a contradiction in this country until you have actually eaten here lmao. Will upload pictues from trips soon!</p>
	</section>

</Base>
